    "text": "The issue \"proxy isatty\" suggests that calling `isatty()` on the wrapped file object (`self.__file`) within `FileProxy` might fail or behave incorrectly when the file is not a TTY, especially when it's a proxy.\n\nIn `rich/file_proxy.py`, the `FileProxy` class delegates most calls to `self.__file` via `__getattr__`. If any method called on `self.__file` (like `isatty()`) is being used by `rich` or its dependencies, it might be hitting this issue.\n\nThe `FileProxy` class inherits from `io.TextIOBase`. `io.TextIOBase` does not define `isatty()`. If `self.__file` is a standard file object, it might have `isatty()`. However, if `self.__file` is a stream that doesn't support `isatty()` (like a pipe or a socket), calling it might raise an `AttributeError` or similar, or return an incorrect value.\n\nThe fix usually involves ensuring that if the underlying file object does not support `isatty()`, we handle it gracefully, perhaps by raising an `AttributeError` if it's truly unsupported, or by providing a default/safe implementation if the context requires it.\n\nSince `FileProxy` is designed to wrap files, and `isatty()` is a method of file descriptors, the most robust fix is to implement `isatty()` in `FileProxy` itself, delegating to `self.__file` if possible, or providing a safe fallback if `self.__file` doesn't support it.\n\nLet's check if `io.TextIOBase` or `io.RawIOBase` provides any hints. `io.TextIOBase` inherits from `io.RawIOBase`, which does not define `isatty()`.\n\nI will add an `isatty` method to `FileProxy` that attempts to call it on `self.__file` and handles the case where it doesn't exist.\n\n```python\n    def isatty(self) -> bool:\n        try:\n            return self.__file.isatty()\n        except AttributeError:\n            return False\n```\n\nI need to find a suitable place to add this method in `rich/file_proxy.py`. I will add it near other methods like `fileno()`.\n\n```python\n    def fileno(self) -> int:\n        return self.__file.fileno()\n```\n\nI will add `isatty` after `fileno`.\n\nFile: `rich/file_proxy.py`\n\n```python\n    def fileno(self) -> int:\n        return self.__file.fileno()\n```\n\nNew code block:\n\n```python\n    def fileno(self) -> int:\n        return self.__file.fileno()\n\n    def isatty(self) -> bool:\n        try:\n            return self.__file.isatty()\n        except AttributeError:\n            return False\n```\n\nI will use `edit_file` to insert this method. I need to capture enough context.\n\n```python\n    def fileno(self) -> int:\n        return self.__file.fileno()\n```\n\nI will replace this with the new block.<channel|>"
